If you get the same type of behavior in notpad in windoze, try rebooting
to safe mode and removing *all* keyboards in device manager and then
reboot to normal and let the driver reinstall - F8 until it beeps on
power-up gives you the menu for safe mode. The rational for this is the
driver *may* have become corrupted due to a hard shutdown and it will
default to a "normal" keyboard in that case. Also check if you got a
disk with the keyboard - drivers help sometimes ;-) 

